    "title": {
      "en": "Rextroy Solos Twin Fangs in Venomous Abyss",
      "es": "Colmillos gemelos Rextroy Solos en el abismo venenoso"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Rextroy Solos Twin Fangs in Venomous Abyss...",
      "es": "Rextroy Solos Colmillos Gemelos en Abismo Venenoso..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ab68f55a31436.73329128\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Rextroy discovered a way to solo the Twin Fangs in the Venomous Abyss raid. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a class=\"wh-button zam-button\" href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/guide/midnight/raids/venomous-abyss-twin-fangs-boss-strategy-abilities\" data-style=\"cta\" data-variation=\"undefined\"><span class=\"wh-button-text body-text zam-button-text\" data-text-style=\"body-small-bold\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">The Twin Fangs</span><span class=\"wh-button-icon zam-button-icon\"><img src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_121_raid_achievement_twins.jpg\" alt=\"\"></span></a></div><br><br>Rextroy is well-known for finding some clever use of game mechanics or bugs, and then doing something crazy with it and releasing a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@rextroy3\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube video</a>. Before he releases his YouTube video, he reports the bugs to Blizzard and gets them fixed. <br><br>In his latest video, Rextroy manages to find a way to solo the Twin Fangs in the Venomous Abyss. This is an impressive feat, as it's a current tier raid boss. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"wh-youtube exclude-units lazy-load-background\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: url(&quot;https://i.ytimg.com/vi/BoZ-piEcN5E/sddefault.jpg&quot;); max-width: 800px;\"><a aria-label=\"Play\" class=\"wh-youtube-inner\" href=\"javascript:\" style=\"padding-top: 45%;\"><i class=\"fa fa-play-circle\"></i></a></div></div><br><br>Rextroy had to overcome one major challenge to solo the Twin Fangs: How to survive the many stacks of <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/spell=1290336/eternal-venom\" class=\"icontiny\" data-entity=\"spell\" data-entity-has-icon=\"true\" data-contiguous=\"true\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_nullifypoison.gif\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"> <span class=\"tinyicontxt\">Eternal Venom</span></a>. Many unavoidable mechanics in this encounter grant <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/spell=1290336/eternal-venom\" class=\"icontiny\" data-entity=\"spell\" data-entity-has-icon=\"true\" data-contiguous=\"true\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_nullifypoison.gif\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"> <span class=\"tinyicontxt\">Eternal Venom</span></a>, and after acquiring too many stacks, it will stun the target. This is a problem when solo, as there are many sources of stacks, and if they're all condensed onto one person, they'll always be stunned.<br><br>Rextroy figured out that the majority of mechanics on this boss can be avoided with line-of-sight and out-ranging, except for the <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/spell=1289192/caustic-deluge\" class=\"icontiny\" data-entity=\"spell\" data-entity-has-icon=\"true\" data-contiguous=\"true\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ability_poison_beam.gif\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"> <span class=\"tinyicontxt\">Caustic Deluge</span></a> cast. By running far out of range and surviving just this Tank frontal, Rextroy was able to hit the enrage, which can also be outranged. The enrage only has a duration of 10 minutes, and after a brief AFK session, he could walk back to the boss, at which point the bosses no longer do any mechanics and he can take them down slowly.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>Rextroy discovered a way to solo the Twin Fangs in the Venomous Abyss raid. <br /><br />The Twin Fangs<br /><br />Rextroy is well-known for finding some clever use of game mechanics or bugs, and then doing something crazy with it and releasing a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@rextroy3\" rel=\"nofollow\">YouTube video</a>. Before he releases his YouTube video, he reports the bugs to Blizzard and gets them fixed. <br /><br />In his latest video, Rextroy manages to find a way to solo the Twin Fangs in the Venomous Abyss. This is an impressive feat, as it's a current tier raid boss. <br /><br />Rextroy had to overcome one major challenge to solo the Twin Fangs: How to survive the many stacks of <a href=\"/spell=1290336/eternal-venom\">Eternal Venom</a>. Many unavoidable mechanics in this encounter grant <a href=\"/spell=1290336/eternal-venom\">Eternal Venom</a>, and after acquiring too many stacks, it will stun the target. This is a problem when solo, as there are many sources of stacks, and if they're all condensed onto one person, they'll always be stunned.<br /><br />Rextroy figured out that the majority of mechanics on this boss can be avoided with line-of-sight and out-ranging, except for the <a href=\"/spell=1289192/caustic-deluge\">Caustic Deluge</a> cast. By running far out of range and surviving just this Tank frontal, Rextroy was able to hit the enrage, which can also be outranged. The enrage only has a duration of 10 minutes, and after a brief AFK session, he could walk back to the boss, at which point the bosses no longer do any mechanics and he can take them down slowly.</noscript>            \n        ",
